    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nerva</span></b> , ae, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman family name of
				the</i> Licinii, Cocceii, <i>and</i> Silii. So M.
			Cocceius Nerva, <i>the Roman
			emperor</i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nervĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the emperor Nerva, Nervian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miles,</span>”
				<i>of the Nervian legion</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. B. Gild. 421</span></i>
			.</div>
